            <title>[LU-21176] sanity test_230q: FAIL: stripe hash none</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21176</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;sanity test_230q (dir auto split) fails in interop "custom" review sessions (master servers, older-branch clients) with:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;  Update not seen after 10s: want 'crush,fixed' got 'none'&lt;br/&gt;
  sanity test_230q: FAIL: stripe hash none&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The test creates 150 then 300 files, expects the directory to auto split to 'crush' and then 'crush,fixed', and 'lfs getdirstripe -H' still reports 'none' after the wait.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Seen on the lustre-reviews custom interop sessions (b2_15 and b2_16 clients with master servers) of change 70636 (sessions bf404d6d-3ec0-45ac-8508-078b4dc5a1b7 and c76b3293-c934-4481-be67-e40e5c167e0d, 2026-11-09), and on unrelated changes 70566 (2026-11-08), 68609 (2026-09-03) and 66882 (2026-09-02). Rainshadow finds 21 failures with this error since 2025-01-17, none linked to a ticket. It is not seen in the master review-ldiskfs, DNE or master-next runs of the test with this error. The existing tickets for 230q cover other errors ("stripe count N != N": &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20840" title="DNE auto-split: stripe cap uses inflated mdt_mds_mds_conns (-E2BIG), failed splits EX-lock dir repeatedly, migration blocks clients" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20840"&gt;LU-20840&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-14058" title="Create tests for large number of MDTs" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-14058"&gt;LU-14058&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-15844" title="sanity test_230q: FAIL: stripe count  != 2 " class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-15844"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-15844&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Change 70636 touches EC/OST layout code only, not MDT directory auto split.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Raised by Patch Watcher run pw-engineer-70636-ps1-58a3a7556ba2 on &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/70636" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/70636&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
